{"id":"jim-s-three-count","pid":"hg:jim-s-three-count","name":"Jim's three count","chapter":"Tricks in three count / causal diagrams","kind":"pattern","page":26,"label":"25","jugglers":2,"objects":null,"timing":null,"pdf":"book/highgate.pdf#page=26&view=FitH,779","passist":null,"passist_candidate":null,"passist_fork":{"url":"https://pass.algrant.ca/siteswap/7p04060607p06060.07p060607p040606?jugglers=2&hands=Ar-_-Al-_._-Br-_-Bl","kind":"staggered","names":["A","B"]},"notations":[],"derived":{"kind":"global-4hss","value":"7746666","global":"77466667746666","confidence":"low","matches_stated":null},"body":[{"t":"p","h":"Jim&#x27;s three count is a variation on three count created by Jim Brennan. In Jim&#x27;s three count one person always throws crossing passes. It&#x27;s very easy to draw a causal diagram for this pattern, you just take a causal diagram for three count and relabel some of the beats."},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"p","h":"In this diagram all of Anne&#x27;s passes are right to left or left to right throws, so they&#x27;re straight passes. However Ben&#x27;s passes are right to right or left to left throws, so they&#x27;re crossing passes. Note that after her first pass, Anne&#x27;s first self is with the same hand. This is a hurry. The self throws after Anne&#x27;s third pass, and Ben&#x27;s second and fourth passes are also hurries."},{"t":"p","h":"You can create lots of patterns by relabelling the beats on causal diagrams. Here&#x27;s another three count variation where both jugglers throw crossing passes."},{"t":"d","i":1},{"t":"p","h":"This pattern is a bit collision prone because Anne throws a crossing right hand pass at the same time as Ben throws a crossing left hand pass (and vice-versa). Note also that Ben&#x27;s first left hand beat has no arrow pointing to it, but an arrow pointing away from it. This shows that he starts with two clubs in his left hand."},{"t":"p","h":"There is another way to draw a causal diagram for Jim&#x27;s three count."},{"t":"d","i":2},{"t":"p","h":"In this variation Ben starts half a beat after Anne and both jugglers throw floaty single passes. This slows the whole pattern down and also eliminates the hurries. In this pattern it&#x27;s quite hard to keep half a beat out of phase! One way to maintain the half beat difference is to flip the clubs that are shown as holds in the diagram."}],"drawings":[{"file":"p26-1.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":4.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":5.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":6.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":9.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":11.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":12.0,"hand":"R"}]},{"juggler":"B","name":"Ben","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":4.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":5.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":6.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":7.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":8.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":9.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":11.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":12.0,"hand":"R"}]}],"arrows":[{"from":[0,0.0,"R"],"to":[1,1.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,1.0,"R"],"to":[0,2.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,2.0,"L"],"to":[0,3.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,3.0,"R"],"to":[1,4.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,4.0,"L"],"to":[0,5.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,5.0,"R"],"to":[0,6.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,6.0,"L"],"to":[1,7.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,7.0,"L"],"to":[0,8.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,8.0,"R"],"to":[0,9.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,9.0,"L"],"to":[1,10.0,"R"]},{"from":[0,10.0,"R"],"to":[0,11.0,"L"]},{"from":[0,11.0,"L"],"to":[0,12.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,0.0,"R"],"to":[0,1.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,1.0,"L"],"to":[1,2.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,2.0,"R"],"to":[1,3.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,3.0,"L"],"to":[0,4.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,4.0,"L"],"to":[1,5.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,5.0,"R"],"to":[1,6.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,6.0,"L"],"to":[0,7.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,7.0,"R"],"to":[1,8.0,"L"]},{"from":[1,8.0,"L"],"to":[1,9.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,9.0,"R"],"to":[0,10.0,"R"]},{"from":[1,10.0,"R"],